# Copy to .env, chmod 600, and fill in. Never commit this file.
#
# BETTER: do not use this file on the appliance at all. Run
#
#     ./scripts/setup_credential.sh
#
# which puts the key in secrets/anthropic-key and has systemd hand it over as
# a credential. The key is then never in the process environment, so not in
# /proc/<pid>/environ, not inherited by mpv, yt-dlp, wmctrl or xdotool, and
# not picked up by a tar of this directory. That last one is not hypothetical.
#
# This file remains useful for one thing: running uvicorn by hand from a
# terminal, where no unit file is involved. core/provider.py reads it directly
# as its last fallback.
#
# Left EMPTY on purpose. A placeholder like sk-ant-... is worse than nothing:
# the code sees a non-empty key and you get a 401 from Anthropic instead of
# the clear local "no API key" message it goes to the trouble of writing.
ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=
